<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Respiratory Physiology</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the principle of pulmonary ventilation, including the driving forces and resistance, intrapulmonary pressure and intrapleural pressure, pulmonary surfactant.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand lung volumes and lung capacities, minute ventilation and alveolar ventilation.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the principle of gas exchange in the lungs and its influencing factors, ventilation / perfusion ratio.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the oxygen-binding capacity, oxygen content, oxygen-hemoglobin dissociation curve and its influencing factors.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the control of breathing.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Gastrointestinal physiology</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the slow wave of smooth muscle in gastrointestinal tract and their innervation. Gastrointestinal regulatory substances.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the digestion process and its regulation in the stomach and small intestine.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the peristalsis of smooth muscle in GI tract.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Know the main absorptive region and the absorption process of nutrients in small intestine.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Energy Metabolism and Body Temperature</strong></span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand energy metabolism and some key concepts (thermal equivalent of oxygen and respiratory quotient).</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the factors affecting energy metabolism, concept and significance of specific dynamic action.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the concept, normal value, physiological variations and significance of basal metabolic rate.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand the concept and physiological variations of body temperature, and the mechanism of body temperature regulation.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Know the heat production and heat loss process.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Sense Organs</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Purpose and requirement:</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To understand the functions of various sense organs.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To master the general characteristics of sensory receptors, vision and hearing.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Teaching contents</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Basic concepts:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master general characteristics of sensory receptors: sensory threshold and adequate stimulus, transducer function of sensory receptors, coding of sensory information, adaptation.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand concept and classification of sensory receptors and sense organs.</span></p>
<ol start="2">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Visual sense organs:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master visual acuity accommodation reflex, near point of vision, papillary light reflex, cone system and rod system, transduction of light energy by rod, cones and color vision. Trichromatic theory of vision, dark and light adaptation, visual field.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand anatomical basis of eye, optical principle relative to formation of an image in eye, reduced eye, and structure of retina, chemistry of rhodopsin, space vision and binocular vision.</span></p>
<ol start="3">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Auditory sense organs:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master pathways of transmitting sound wave from external environment to inner ear, increasing sound pressure by auditory ossicles and tympanic membrane, vibrations of basilar membrane and traveling wave theory, bioelectrical phenomenon of the cochlea.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand structure of ear, collecting sound of auricle, resonance of auditory canal, function of Eustachian tube pharyntotympanic tube), basic structure of cochlea, action potential in auditory nerve, auditory thresholds and audible area.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Endocrine System</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Purpose and Requirement</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To understand importance of endocrine system in regulation of physiological functions.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To master the actions of several important hormones and regulation of their secretion.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Teaching contents</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Overview:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master concepts of hormone and endocrine system, chemical classification and actions of hormones, general characteristics of hormonal actions.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand formation, storage, release and transport of hormones, mechanisms of hormone action: hypothesis of the second messenger and hypothesis of the genes.</span></p>
<ol start="2">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Endocrine function of hypothalamus:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master functional relationship between hypothalamus and pituitary gland: hypothalamic hypophysial portal system and hypothalamo- hypophysial nerve tract, actions of several important hypothalamic regulating peptides: THR, GnRH, GHRIH, CRH, and GHRH.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand classification and functional characteristics of the neuro-endocrine neurons in hypothalamus.</span></p>
<ol start="3">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Pituitary:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master biological effects of adenohypophysial hormone (GH, PRL) and regulation of their secretion, actions of neurohypophysial hormones (vasopressin and oxytocin) and regulation of their secretion.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand morphological characteristics of adenohypophysial cells, structure and biosynthesis of neurohypophysial hormones.</span></p>
<ol start="4">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Thyroid:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master biological effects of thyroid hormone, regulation of thyroid hormone secretion.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand biosynthesis of thyroid hormone and iodine metabolism.</span></p>
<ol start="5">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Adrenal Gland:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master actions of glucocorticoids and mineralocorticoid, regulation of their secretion, hormones (norepinephrine and epinephrine) produced by adrenal medulla and their actions as well as regulation of section.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand synthesis and metabolism of glucocoricoids, mineralo-corticoida, norepinephrine and epinephrine.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;"><strong>Reproduction</strong></span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Purpose and Requirement</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To master the major endocrine functions of sexual glands, actions of sex hormones.</span></li>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">To understand the processes of spermatogenesis and progenesis. Menstrual cycle, main steps of pregnancy.</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Teaching contents</span></p>
<ol>
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Male reproduction:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master testicular function: spermatogenesis by testes, actions of testosterone, regulation of testicular<strong> </strong>function: hypothalamic pituitary-Leydig cell axis and hypthalamic-pituitary seminiferous tubule axis.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand endocrine functions of testes: synthesis and metabolism of testosterone</span></p>
<ol start="2">
<li><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Female reproduction:</span></li>
</ol>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Master physiological effects and mechanism of estrogens and progesterone; regulation of ovarian function: hypothalamic- pituitary- ovarian axis.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">Understand ovulation, menstrual cycle, processes of pregnancy: fertilization, implantation, maintenance of pregnancy. Parturition and lactation</span></p></font></span><b style="mso-bidi-font-weight:normal"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;mso-ansi-font-weight:bold;
font-size:10.5000pt;mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></b></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr style="height:26.2000pt;">
                <td width=777 valign=center colspan=14 style="width:466.7000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
